ow about the shipping company?\" [990] \"Shipping company? What's that supposed to mean?\" [991] \"Just to see if there's any drama,\" Peachins murmured. [992] Forty-five minutes later, the sergeant put down the phone, wiping his brow with a trembling handkerchief. He finally sighed: \"Well, the show's about to start. It's too absurd... You know what the shipping company's manager just told me?\" [993] \"Oh, Dad,\" Peachins said, \"you're teasing us. What did he say?\" [994] \"There's no Hamnet Sedra on the passenger list!\" [995] They all looked at each other in surprise. Then Gordon Rowe whistled, putting out his cigarette in the sergeant's ashtray. \"So that's it,\" he murmured. \"The famous Dr. Sedra...\"\n[996] \"Good, I like it,\" Percy murmured. \"I like it a lot.\" [997] \"Good heavens, he's a fake!\" Sam exclaimed, \"Listen, kid, you can't tell a soul. Not a word, or else I'll\u2014\"\n[998] \"Alright, alright, sergeant,\" Reine interrupted him gently, leaning back on the leather sofa with many wrinkles on his forehead, \"Don't be in such a hurry. A good set-up doesn't necessarily make a good play, and a suspicious situation can't convict someone. Why did you describe Sedra to the secretary?\" [999] \"Well,\" Sam snorted, \"he checked the passenger list and couldn't find the guy's name. I described Sedra to the secretary and asked him to check with the ship's staff. The ship docked this morning, and they're all still on duty, so he did it right away. Well, Sedra not only isn't on the passenger list, but no one remembers anyone on board who looks like Sedra!\" [1000] \"Interesting,\" Rowe pondered. [1001] \"I admit the strange smell has grown stronger,\" muttered the old gentleman, \"strange, very strange\u2026\"\n[1002] \"Can't you see what this means?\" Percy exclaimed, \"It means that Sedra has been in the country at least four days!\" [1003] \"How did you figure that out, Percy?\" his father asked. [1004] \"He didn't fly across the Atlantic, did he? You 